<title>USA: Rhone-Poulenc's Zagam approved by FDA.</title>
<headline>Rhone-Poulenc's Zagam approved by FDA.</headline>
<dateline>COLLEGEVILLE, Penn. 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer Inc said on Friday the U.S. Food and Drug Administration has given marketing clearance for Zagam, its oral antibiotic for certain types of pneumonia and bronchitis.</p>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc said Zagam demonstrated activity in clinical trials against a broad range of pathogens causing common lower respiratory tract infections.</p>
<p>Zagam, which is indicated for the treatment of adults 18 and older, will be available in pharmacies nationwide in first quarter 1997, the company said.</p>
</text>
